#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# engineering_form

#% text
# `engineering_form(x)` shows the number `x` in scientific notation with an exponent that is a multiple of 3; `engineering_form(x, n)` with `n` significant digits.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The argument is evaluated first; `engineering_form` stays around the value as a display wrapper. The wrapper stays around the value: it is a display directive and changes no computation.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
engineering_form(12345.6789)
#% output
#= engineering_form(12345.6789)

#% cell
engineering_form(0.000123)
#% output
#= engineering_form(0.000123)

#% cell
engineering_form(1.0e9, 3)
#% output
#= engineering_form(1000000000.0, 3)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `scientific_form`, `number_form`, `decimal_form`
